Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-30-2001||03:54 PM||||Origionally when I had my alarm "professionally" installed, it ended up looking like it was installed by a inbred monkey that was colorblind..<P>Wires were taped to other colored wires to make it longer,etc<P>(wires were ripped from the fuse box where the "inbred monkey" origionally installed it, so I cant see where "it" put them.)<P><BR>Trying to rewire it again from scratch.. got a question though.. where is the park light relay? (as seen in picture)<P>Thanks<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/plrelay.jpg"> <P><BR>For anyone wondering where it was installed, It was installed at Wacky Wheatleys here in PEI.. they wont look at it again since its not "this years model" and dont have their repair book on it anymore.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||10-30-2001||07:32 PM||||I do believe that the fiero never came with a park lamp relay in its circuit (the curent goes through the switch),  The alarm system is unable to deliver current for park lamps, but only signal to a relay. So you will have to wire in your own relay. Park lamps cicuit is the brown wire that comes out of the back of the switch (terminal E) Your relay will give this wire battery voltage. You can buy a simple 4 wire relay at any automotive supply store. and use the wire from your alarm as the positive signal feed to relay.||||reg||1
Z||000002||edbone||10-30-2001||08:35 PM||||What the diagram is refering to as a parking light relay output, is actually the relay output comming out of the alarm. The input could be a negative or positive. So whatever you put the pink wire too(+ or -) will come out of the red/white wire. on the fiero, you would have too put the pink wire out of the alarm to a 12v source and the red\white wire to the brown wire on the fiero located behind the parking light switch. Hope this helps,  Eddie||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-30-2001||09:51 PM||||thanks for the info people, I will check into it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||10-31-2001||05:55 AM||||Use the brown wire on the light switch connector, no relay required.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
